During this period, intense wars took place among many aristocrats who fought for the throne and crown.
These Three Kingdoms are considered one of the bloodiest periods in ancient Chinese history, during which thousands of people lost their lives in the struggle to seize the highest throne in the Great Palace in Xi'an.
