Europe is a relatively small continent, but it has many independent countries. Under normal conditions, traveling between numerous countries requires going through visa application and passport control procedures several times.
Nevertheless, the Schengen Area functions like a country in this regard.
As long as you are residing in this region, you can generally cross the borders without having to go through the passport checkpoint again.
Similarly, with a Schengen visa, there is no longer a need to apply for a visa separately for each Schengen member country, thus saving you time, money, and paper.
